==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|rōr}}, from {{inh|de|goh|rōr}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*rauzą}}, of obscure origin; compare {{cog|en|rush}} and {{cog|non|reyrr}}, also possibly related to {{cog|la|ruscum|t=bark}}.

Cognate with {{cog|hrx|Roher}}, {{cog|da|rør}}, {{cog|sv|rör}}.

